    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1fc5bdfa092d69dbe06ee88998a5c128b049413899cb990a53e6149e43051fe0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The restriction a<3/4 recurs at several separately stated proof interfaces: convergence of the Voronoi and Theorem 3 main series, inclusion of the target line in g4's continuation region, absolute convergence of the saddle-point remainder, and convergence needed to remove the outer cut and estimate a final sum. The theorem range is therefore supported by a chain of convergence obligations rather than appearing only as a formal range in the theorem statement.",
