    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6da9f57ac6ed01aa235f82dd4778f6e14d60e1dc126c26dcdab5084f2495fd95",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof first obtains complementary two-variable representations and makes their comparison conditional on continuing the auxiliary function g; only then does it specialize and integrate to reduce the mean-square problem to g on the required slice. The later four-way decomposition discharges that concentrated continuation burden component by component, using absolute convergence for g1 and g2, a separate continuation for g3, and Lemma 2 for g4.",
